This product includes software developed as part of RAW-Diffusion
(Reinders et al.), released under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
https://github.com/SonyResearch/RAW-Diffusion

Modifications made in this work, relative to that code base:

  * the prediction target is changed from RAW Bayer data to HDR RGB radiance,
    optionally reparameterised through the PU21 perceptually uniform encoding;
  * the dataset pipeline is replaced with scene-referred HDR sources and a
    percentile-clipping degradation that synthesises the LDR guidance;
  * the evaluation stack is replaced with the HDR metrics reported in the paper
    (PU21-PSNR, PU21-VSI, PU21-PIQE, HDR-VDP-3 and FID-R) together with the
    brightness alignment and the camera-response correction they are computed
    after.

The guidance encoder follows EDSR (Lim et al.). The spatially-adaptive
normalisation follows SPADE (Park et al.). The PU21 encoding is by Mantiuk and
Azimi; our implementation is checked against the reference release at
https://github.com/gfxdisp/pu21 .
